oh it's been a while since I've gotten  to wear this so this one is a little bit  impromptu and I'm kind of coming at this  topic sideways I want to kind of take a  look in a revisiting eye to christopher  eccleston 'he's time on Doctor Who and  more specifically his departure from the  show and his reluctance to return so  here's what has been known for some time  he made the decision to leave the show  before the first series was done being  shot and that was not supposed to be  made public until that we in advance of  the party of the ways airing but it got  leaked by the BBC and he had some there  was there's been various sort of  unconfirmed nothing direct from either  him or the producers reports of him  clashing with some of the key figures  involved whether it was Russell T Davies  whether was other producers it's it's  it's not worth speculating on and as a  result  Eccleston has been very sparse on Doctor  Who since his departure he has never  come back to appear on screen again  something which David Tennant did do for  the 50th anniversary which is kind of  the thing that a lot of people hoped he  would come back for including Stephen  Moffat the showrunner at the time  because that was his hope until  Christopher Eccleston turned him down  and he ended up creating the war doctor  instead he does do conventions  intermittently he has yet to appear in  Big Finish  which again is some  thing David Tennant has already taken up  the torch doing and many other people  involved in modern era Doctor Who do a  cast of Torchwood wherefore song you  know lots of stuff being done there he  hasn't shown up for that either and I  kind of want to address that because  some things came out recently that I  think give another perspective on this  cuz I think a lot of us had kind of  assumed largely because Christopher  Eccleston has never said flat out what  the conflict was in detail and neither  has anyone else so everyone's kind of  maintaining a level of professionalism  so we don't know exactly what went down  and it was kind of presumed for a while  that he just held a grudge against the  BBC because there was an agreement for  how his departure was supposed to happen  they didn't stick to it and he was just  ticked at them except he's it took a  while but he did start doing BBC related  things again eventually he's never gone  back to Doctor Who though so it does  seem like it's always seemed like there  was something more unique to the show  that made him reluctant to ever come  back and something that came out  recently which I'm not gonna go so far  as to say is the reason that he hasn't  come back but it has given another layer  to it and that is that at the time he  was anorexic he was battling mental and  physical health issues and he maintains  that his the physical state he was in  again at the time being anorexic was  part of how he was able to secure the  job now whether that's true or not he  certainly seems to believe it and the  reason I kind of want to bring attention  is because again like I know there are  some members of the Doctor Who fan  community who  are annoyed and upset with Eccleston's  very limited engagement with the fandom  and like I have friends very  specifically hold a grudge for his not  coming back to the 50th anniversary and  I feel like it's anyone who feels that  way this is important to take on board  because what this means is his coming  back to the show would be about more  than working with the BBC again it would  be about more than working on the show  again because I at this point anyone who  we might have had his issues with  probably isn't working on the show  anymore but it would be him re-entering  a work environment and a character in a  headspace that he occupied while sick  and that is actually asking a lot of  anybody to do so to make a comparison  anyone who's holding a grudge against  Eccleston for not coming back for  something like the 50th anniversary and  for continuing to engage him with the  fandom fairly sporadically and in  limited ways that would be like being  mad at a recovering alcoholic for not  coming to a party you're having at a bar  it'd be nice if they showed up but if  they decide it's better for their own  health for them not to be there not to  be in that space not to be in that  environment because it might bring back  the pain of past trauma physical and  mental then they're within the right to  say no I can't do that and again I don't  want to overstate this because I am  extrapolating out at least a little bit  because Eccleston has not said flat out  that that is part of why he engages with  Doctor Who as little as  does but I still feel like it's worth  having a full appreciation of because it  becomes a reason where now it makes more  sense than what we had them what we knew  previously on its own as far as why he  doesn't come back why he hasn't gotten  involved with Big Finish why he didn't  come back for the fiftieth anniversary  why he might not come back for any  future big anniversaries we might never  get the Ninth Doctor as portrayed by  Christopher Eccleston in anything  outside of his original 13 episodes and  that would be a shame because he was  fantastic he was really good in that  part  he brought a really unique feel to the  role that other actors happened and  whether you feel that he did better or  worse than anyone else that's a matter  of personal taste but what he brought  was very unique and it's something that  I've always kind of wished we could have  had a little bit more of than we got so  I get the frustration at not having more  but if anybody out there still feels a  frustration against Christopher  Eccleston as a person for that I hope  that you'll find it in your heart to  accept that the guy's got a you've got  to take care of himself that's that's  ultimately kind of the first thing that  every person has to do and I don't mean  like act selfishly but I mean like you  have to you have to take care of your  own body your own mind and if you're not  that needs to be addressed and if you  used to not  then it's a good idea to avoid repeating  that situation or you weren't taking  care of yourself properly so I don't  know I just maybe again maybe it is  because I know people personally who do  kind of or have you know maybe in light  of this they've already softened which  would be amazing but who have  historically kind of held a fairly open  grudge against him for his failure to  ever come back and maybe the people I  know who are like that are a vast  minority I mean I kind of hope so but  just in case just remember the guys yet  yes he's an actor but he's also he's a  human being with stuff to work through  and however he needs to do that let him  do it so yeah there we go  suppose it works that um this is coming  out I'm releasing this the same month as  World Mental Health Day so guess that's  about as close to appropriate as I'll  get with this but in any case whatever  your thoughts are on what I've talked  about or any of this drop something down  in the comments and let's talk about it  there's other stuff to do as well the  like to subscribe both of which are  massively helpful link to the my patreon  even more helpful if you feel like Chuck  in a buck a month my way plus there are  other links down there as well click on  them and they'll take you places but you  also don't have to because I am NOT  gonna tell you what you need to do  you'll decide for yourself what's best  for you and until next time this counsel  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

